# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the notes

# The base state and the instruction files ask the engine in force too
# (`EnginePolicy::keep_gate`), but no break of that can be caught: the base
# state is taken as the session starts, before any change of level, and
# for a `.md` file in the workspace `may_store` is the same under every
# engine a session can come to (no level enters it, no such name looks like
# a secret, and `deny` beats `ask` beats `allow`, so an approval for the
# session cannot lift a rule that holds it back). The second review of the
# fixes found the break that stood here surviving.

[break] the-index-keeps-the-engine-of-the-assembly
rule: The index asks the permission engine in force, not the one the session was put together with.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/policy.rs
in: EnginePolicy::index_gate
find: now: Box::new(move || policy.upgrade().map(|policy| policy.engine()))
replace: now: { let engine = self.engine(); Box::new(move || { let _ = &policy; Some(Arc::clone(&engine)) }) }
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it index::the_index_follows_the_engine_in_force_after_a_change_of_level

