    cortex-index extract::tests::a_typescript_module_declared_by_a_string_is_named_by_the_string
    cortex-index::it outlines::typescript

[break] a-regular-expression-is-read-as-code
rule: In JavaScript and TypeScript a `/` where an expression begins opens a regular expression, whose content is blanked as a string's: a `//` or a `/*` in it is not a comment.
file: crates/cortex-index/src/lex.rs
find: regex: true
replace: regex: false
caught-by:
    cortex-index extract::tests::a_regular_expression_with_two_slashes_is_not_a_comment
    cortex-index extract::tests::a_regular_expression_with_slash_star_does_not_open_a_comment
    cortex-index lex::tests::a_regular_expression_is_blanked_as_a_string_and_a_division_is_code
    cortex-index::it outlines::typescript
    cortex-index::it outlines::javascript

[break] every-slash-of-a-line-is-scanned-for-a-regular-expression
rule: After a `/` that looked like a regular expression's start does not close on its line, no later `/` of the line is tried, so a line of them costs linear time.
